  "title": "xinjiegit/ben_27_formalization",
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 and Mathlib proof that there are absolute constants c > 0 and p₀ such that, for every prime p ≥ p₀, the minimum size m(p) of a set A ⊆ 𝔽_p with |A| ≥ 2 and no uniquely represented sum satisfies m(p) ≥ c (log p / log log p)².  Here representations are unordered two-element multisets from A, repeated summands are allowed, and \"no unique sum\" means that every such multiset has a distinct equal-sum mate.",
